# Forms Validation

- One schema ({{zod}}) per form in `lib/validation/`, used on client **and** server.
- Visible labels (placeholder is not a label), `autocomplete` attributes.
- Required fields marked in text, e.g. "Email (required)" — not colour or a lone `*`; when most fields are required, also label optional ones "(optional)".
- Errors: field-level text linked with `aria-describedby`, summary at the top on submit (each item links to its field), focus moves to the summary or first error; keep what the user typed.
- Changing a field never submits or navigates by itself (WCAG 3.2.2); payments, contracts and deletions get a review/confirm or undo step (3.3.4).
- No redundant entry (WCAG 3.3.7); paste allowed everywhere; no CAPTCHA puzzles without an alternative.

## Never
- Validate only on the client
- clear the form on error
- disable submit without saying why
